  "notes": "すてき is a na-adjective expressing genuine admiration for something wonderful or lovely.\n\nWRITING:\nCan be written as {素敵|すてき} but hiragana is common.\n\nFORMS:\n- すてきな + noun: a lovely ~\n- すてきに: wonderfully (adverbial)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- すてきな⟦{服|ふく}→服：00695_fuku⟧: lovely clothes\n- すてきな⟦{考|かんが}え→考え：00855_kangae⟧: wonderful idea\n- すてきな⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧: lovely person\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used by women; expresses genuine positive admiration.\n\nSIMILAR:\n- ⟦{素晴|すば}らしい→素晴らしい：01119_subarashii⟧: wonderful (more emphatic)\n- ⟦きれい→きれい：00717_kirei⟧: beautiful, pretty",
